  <translations>
    <en>
      <description>Rain Bird R-VAN-SST is a rotary nozzle designed to deliver controlled, water-efficient irrigation for landscaped areas. Multiple rotating streams apply water more slowly than many conventional spray nozzles, helping the soil absorb it and reducing runoff when the system is correctly designed. The stated coverage is 1.5 × 9.1 m; the watering pattern is strip; recommended operating pressure is 2.1–3.8 bar.

R-VAN nozzles are useful for matching irrigation coverage to the shape of the planting area, including standard arcs and narrow strips. Select the pattern to suit the location and maintain compatible pressure and flow. Use with compatible Rain Bird 1800/RD1800 spray bodies or other approved bodies as specified by the manufacturer.

Actual radius and uniformity depend on pressure, spacing, soil and wind conditions.</description>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h1s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Rotary nozzle for narrow strips and corners</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p1s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Rain Bird R-VAN-SST</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p1s1</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text> is a rotary nozzle with a dedicated pattern for narrow rectangular spaces. It is designed for strips alongside paths, fences and lawn edges where a standard circular spray would extend beyond the intended area.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h2s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Coverage dimensions and operating data</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p2s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Technical data: </text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p2s1</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>pattern странична ивица; coverage 1.5 × 9.1 m; operating pressure 2.1–3.8 bar, recommended 3.1 bar. Flow is 1.36–2.12 L/min, depending on system pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h3s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Adjusting the spray pattern</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p3s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Adjustment: </text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p3s1</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>coverage size and boundaries are adjusted while the system is running. The multi-stream rotary pattern produces larger droplets, and tool-free adjustment helps match the spray to the strip outline.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h4s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Choosing left, right or side-strip coverage</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p4s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>LCS creates a left-corner strip, RCS a right-corner strip, and SST a long side strip. Select the pattern according to the sprinkler position; left- and right-corner models are not interchangeable.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h5</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-h5s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Design, installation and maintenance</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p5</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p5s0</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>For system design: </text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>4f4a7e6b-7df5-4ee4-94f1-346b68fc75a9-en-p5s1</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>check pressure at the nozzle and position neighbouring zones to avoid dry gaps or overspray onto paving. For optimum operation, Rain Bird recommends an 1800 PRS-45 body at 3.1 bar. Explore </text>
